posts.body:
@BloodyKun
I think the idea of a sandbox for experiments is very useful, although it is difficult to keep everything in one place. It is inevitable to create another area for the project to progress.
@Lionbarrel
I believe that development should be concentrated and only then the results obtained should be released. There are people who make up a game in such a way that they can create exaggerated expectations.
@lavendermocha
I am doing something similar. The game's setting, where the story takes place, is something primary, it is like choosing the world where the characters' adventures will take place. However, I think that a solid system can be applied to any setting. Something very similar to RPG board games.
@gstv87
You brought up interesting subjects, but I believe that this is more for post-production, where you can measure the amount of data existing in the game, whether the game is worth selling or free, whether it is good enough to be hosted online. I use RPG Maker MV where I was able to have a long project, but it should have the same fate as my previous projects. I think that something multiplatform like PC games and mobile games should be made in different versions.
